
Site-specific suite files.

1) <SITE>/suite-adds.rc
 
    This file is included at the END of the suite.rc file to add site-specific
    settings to the core suite definition, e.g. all site-specific [runtime]
    settings, and any site-specific additions to the core suite graph.

2) <SITE>/suite-vars.rc 

    This file is included at the TOP of the suite.rc file to define
    site-specific logical switches used in the core suite definition. Note
    however, these should be avoided in favour of using 1) where possible.
   
Additionally, site "add" files can load private include files. Their filenames
should begin with "_" to distinguish from the general site files above, e.g.:
   site/niwa-ibm-pwr6/
     suite-vars.rc
     suite-adds.rc  # includes site/niwa-ibm-pwr6/_netcdf.rc
     _netcdf.rc  # <--
Where _netcdf.rc adds a netcdf post-processing workflow to the suite, at NIWA.
